.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# local secrets
.env.local
.env
.venv/
results/_test/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
results/playwright-report/
results/playwright-artifacts/
package-lock.json
results/spend.json.lock

# The operator worklist. Live state, not a scored record: it is rewritten on
# every submit, holds the full case text of whatever was dropped in, and would
# conflict on every pull in a deployment that also runs denials. results/
# is committed for predictions, run.json, matrix.md, spend.json and
# spend_plan.md -- the queue is none of those.
results/queue/

# The parked-case worklist, live state for the same reason as the queue:
# answering a parked case rewrites inbox/ and inbox_resolved/ at runtime, so a
# deployment that resumes one case dirties a tracked file and its next pull
# has to pick a winner -- the exact failure mode the ledger split fixed. The
# scored record of every park is in each run's committed predictions/.
results/inbox/
results/inbox_resolved/

# The live spend ledger. Every running server appends to it, so tracking it
# made two deployments edit one file and a pull silently drop real spend. The
# committed record is results/spend_record.json, refreshed deliberately with
# `make record-spend`; this file is seeded from it on first use.
results/spend.json

# Private HOME for the resolver's CLI subprocess (tools/cli_guard.py).
# Holds the CLI's own state files; must never hold a login.
.cli-home/

# Generated from CMS's quarterly PTP edit file by tools/fetch_ncci_ptp.py.
# Deployment-local DATA, not source, for two reasons: the values must come
# from the CMS file each deployment actually downloaded (never from a commit
# someone could edit), and the file is CPT-derived content under the AMA
# licence CMS gates downloads behind -- committing it to a hosted repo would
# be redistribution. Each deployment generates its own.
reference/runtime/10-ncci-ptp-therapy.md
